# Generate symmetry-adapted polynomial basis functions (1st-3rd order)

crystod-group --generate-basis --point-group m-3m

============================================================
  1st order (linear) basis functions
============================================================
* Decomposition *
 1.0 [T1u]
* Irreducible representations for basis functions *
  T1u: [x, y, z]

============================================================
  2nd order (quadratic) basis functions
============================================================
* Decomposition *
 1.0 [A1g] + 1.0 [Eg] + 1.0 [T2g]
* Irreducible representations for basis functions *
  A1g: [x^2 + y^2 + z^2]
  Eg: [-2 x^2 + y^2 + z^2, x^2 - 2 y^2 + z^2]
  T2g: [xy, yz, xz]

============================================================
  3rd order (cubic) basis functions
============================================================
* Decomposition *
 1.0 [A2u] + 2.0 [T1u] + 1.0 [T2u]
* Irreducible representations for basis functions *
  A2u: [xyz]
  T1u: [x^3, y^3, z^3, x^2 y + yz^2, x^2 z + y^2 z, xy^2 + xz^2]
  T2u: [-x^2 y + yz^2, -x^2 z + y^2 z, -xy^2 + xz^2]

(characters and closed-space sections omitted here -- run the command to see them)



# Space-group mode at a k point; --order restricts to a single order
crystod-group --generate-basis --space-group Pm-3m --kpoint 0 0 0 --order 2

============================================================
  2nd order (quadratic) basis functions
============================================================
* Decomposition *
 1.0 [GM1+(1)] + 1.0 [GM3+(2)] + 1.0 [GM5+(3)]
* Irreducible representations for basis functions *
  GM1+(1): [x^2 + y^2 + z^2]
  GM3+(2): [-2 x^2 + y^2 + z^2, x^2 - 2 y^2 + z^2]
  GM5+(3): [xy, yz, xz]
